{"name":"Bright Chartreuse","hex":"#dfff11","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bright","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Emitting much light; visually dazzling; luminous, lucent, radiant.","Of light: brilliant, intense."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Brightness, glow.\n\n Glory, splendour.","Brightness, glow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bright"},{"term":"chartreuse","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A yellow or green liqueur made by Carthusian monks.","A greenish-yellow color."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a bright yellowish-green colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chartreuse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chartreuse (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Chartreuse is a color between yellow and green also referred to as yellow-green or greenish yellow. It was named because of its resemblance to the French liqueur green chartreuse, introduced in 1764. Similarly, chartreuse yellow is a yellow color mixed with a small amount of green, named after the drink yellow chartreuse. The wavelength and frequency of chartreuse is near 547.5 nm or 547.5 THz."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/RAF-Cardington-Shed02_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-RAF-Cardington-Shed02_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chartreuse_(color)","wikidata":"Q1153119"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Catopsilia_pomona_by_kadavoor.JPG/500px-Catopsilia_pomona_by_kadavoor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Catopsilia_pomona_by_kadavoor.JPG/1280px-Catopsilia_pomona_by_kadavoor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Catopsilia_pomona_by_kadavoor.JPG/500px-Ca